Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Non Gyn Cytology Report        Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  45   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  WRN 219  PATH FINE NEEDLE  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 10 15  Results to   Michele Annette Gadd MD  Joseph Misdraji MD      FINAL DIAGNOSIS    A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Satisfactory for evaluation     INTERPRETATION   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANT CELLS     DIAGNOSIS   Adenocarcinoma  consistent with ductal carcinoma of mammary origin   Background of blood and necrosis         Electronically Signed Out By  Rebecca Ann Osgood MD    Diane Kuebler  CT ASCP     By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       RAPID INTERPRETATION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT   FNA Rapid Interpretation     Ductal carcinoma     Pathologist  Joseph Misdraji  M D   FNA performed by  Joseph Misdraji  M D         PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Patient Evaluation and Management  with Interpretation       Chief Complaint  This 45 year old female was referred to the fine needle  aspiration clinic by Dr  Gadd for consultation and diagnosis of a left breast     Clinical History  Patient noted breast lump     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the left breast shows a 1cm irregular nodule  about 0 5cm form areola  at 2 00       Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  verbal consent was obtained  3 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  1 slide was stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Ultrasound was used for evaluation of the lesion     Ultrasound Findings  Small hypoechoic lesion     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Gadd in person at 4  o clock P M       The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Joseph Misdraji MD on REMOVED_DATE 18 20       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast lump noted by patient         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 4 slides in ETOH           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Not Done.
