  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm unoriented lumpectomy specimen  with a needle localization wire in place  The entire specimen is inked black and serially sectioned  There is a surgical staple within a very poorly defined irregular tan pink REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm mass  which extends to within 0 1cm of the margin  Representative sections from this area are submitted in cassettes A F  The remainder of the tissue shows yellow tan fat and tan white  apparently unremarkable fibrous tissue  Representatives section is submitted in cassette G J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of unoriented tan pink fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is sectioned revealing apparently unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  which is submitted entirely in cassettes K P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved superior margin   are two unoriented tan pink fibrofatty soft tissue fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented fibrofatty portion of tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan white fibrous tissue with no gross abnormality  The entire specimen is submitted in cassette S X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented tan pink portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is serially sectioned revealing unremarkable fibrous tissue  The entire specimen is submitted in cassette Y CC  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional medial breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  which is unoriented  The margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned revealing tan white unremarkable fibrous tissue interspersed with yellow tan adipose tissue  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes DD MM  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary fat pad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of yellow tan fat  containing lymph nodes  There is a suture designated as the highest axillary fat  Several possible lymph nodes from this area are submitted in cassette N  Additional possible nodes from the upper third of the axillary fat pad are submitted in cassette OO  The lymph nodes from the middle third are submitted in cassette PP and QQ  The lymph nodes from the lower third are submitted in cassettes RR and SS  Resident  PAUL N  STAATS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Janey Sue Pratt  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR  EXCISION PART C  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR  EXCISION PART D  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL  EXCISION PART E  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL  EXCISION PART F  BREAST LEFT ADDITIONAL MEDIAL  EXCISION PART G  LYMPH NODES LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION , Not Done.
